57,-87.64646,"Halsted, around 18th and 19th","2nd Fri Gallery nights","","","","r","Studios in East Pilsen open their doors for an annual weekend-long festival. Even if the art does not resonate with you, it is worth visiting for the chance to explore the interesting physical spaces, from century-old sunken gardens to…"],["Fiesta del Sol","activity",41.8524,-87.65885,"1000-1600 West Cermak Road, between Loomis and Morgan","late July or early August","","","","r","Fiesta del Sol is an annual fundraising event organized by the Pilsen Neighbors Community Council that has been held annually since 1972. Over the years it has evolved from a block party into a nationally publicized event with corporate…"],["Carnitas Don Pedro","restaurant",41.85777,-87.65384,"1113 W 18th St","Mon-Fri 6AM-6PM, Sat 6AM-5PM, Sun 6AM-3PM","","","","r","No frills and somewhat inconveniently located, but well worth the effort to get there, with some of the most flavorful carnitas in Chicago."],["Tacos Palacio","restaurant",41.85902,-87.64689,"1700 S Halsted St","7AM-8:30PM daily","","","","r","Perhaps the best taquería in Pilsen, so if you don't intend to have a sit-down multi-course meal, head straight here to grab some dirt cheap, incredible tacos."],["Honky Tonk BBQ","restaurant",41.85785,-87.65659,"1213 W 18th St","Tue-Fri 4PM-2AM, Sat 4PM-3AM, Sun 4PM-2AM; kitchen closes at 11PM","","","","r","Exactly what it sounds like — the speakers deliver honky tonk music, while the kitchen serves pulled pork sandwiches, beef briskets, rib tips, and cornbread. There's a full bar as well, with live music on Thursdays and weekends."],["HaiSous","restaurant",41.85786,-87.65356,"1800 S Carpenter St","Mon-Fri 5PM-11PM; Sat 10AM-3PM, Mon-11PM; Sun 10AM-3PM","","","","r","Highly-rated upscale Vietnamese restaurant, known for its modern interpretation of traditional Vietnamese cuisine."],["Kristoffer's Cafe and Bakery","bar",41.85815,-87.64645,"1733 S Halsted St","Mon 7:30AM-3PM, Tue-Fri 7:30AM-5PM, Sat Sun 8AM-4PM","","","","r","A warm, large space with a range of sandwiches, drinks, and baked goods. (They call their seven varieties of tres leches cakes a family specialty.) You will find free Wi-Fi and flyers for every art opening in the area."],["Simone's","bar",41.85814,-87.65104,"960 W 18th St","Sun-Fri 11:30AM-2AM, Sat 11:30AM-3AM","","","","r","Good food (especially the Mexican-influenced Pilsen Burger), but go for the beer: while their mixed drinks cost more than Skylark and aren't nearly as strong, they have an absolutely spectacular collection of beers on tap and in…"]]}